target: constraints/artifacts
version: 1
validations:
  - name: artifacts-core-tests-pass
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run pytest {output_dir}/intentc/core -q"

  - name: artifacts-build-tests-pass
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run pytest {output_dir}/intentc/build -q"

  - name: artifacts-self-check-still-passes
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run intentc check"

  - name: artifacts-prompts-carry-section
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "grep -l '{artifacts}' {output_dir}/intentc/build/agents/prompts/build.prompt {output_dir}/intentc/build/agents/prompts/validate.prompt {output_dir}/intentc/build/agents/prompts/plan.prompt | wc -l | grep -qx 3"

  - name: artifacts-parsed-and-resolved
    type: agent_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      rubric: |
        Verify the core models define an Artifact type (path, kind, note, owner,
        resolved_paths) and that IntentFile, ProjectIntent and Implementation carry an
        `artifacts` list. Verify tests show: (1) a frontmatter `artifacts` list with a
        mapping entry and a string-shorthand entry parses, and inline body references
        are appended as kind "reference", while an inline link to another .ic or
        .icv file is NOT turned into an artifact (it stays in file_references only)
        and produces no undeclared-artifact warning; (2) `artifacts` that is not a list, an entry
        without `path`, and a non-string `kind` each produce a ParseError naming the
        `artifacts` field; (3) load_project expands globs into resolved_paths relative
        to the declaring file and rejects a path that escapes intent/; (4)
        Project.artifacts_for returns target, ancestor, project and implementation
        artifacts in that order, deduplicated; (5) write_project copies artifact files
        and load_project on the copy returns equal artifacts.

  - name: artifacts-drive-staleness-and-sandbox
    type: agent_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      rubric: |
        Verify builder tests show that after a successful build of a feature that
        declares an artifact, editing only the artifact file (not the .ic or .icv)
        makes detect_outdated() report the feature and the next build() rebuilds it
        without force. Verify the converse for inline references: a feature whose
        body links a file it does not declare has source_files() equal to just its
        .ic/.icv files, so editing that file does NOT make it outdated, and
        check_project warns that the reference is undeclared. Verify that the sandbox read paths handed to the agent profile
        include the absolute resolved path of every artifact returned by
        artifacts_for(target), including a project-level artifact, and that the
        BuildContext passed to the mock agent carries the same artifacts.

  - name: artifacts-rendered-in-prompts
    type: agent_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      rubric: |
        Verify render_prompt supplies an `{artifacts}` variable that renders "(none)"
        for an empty list, and otherwise one block per artifact containing the
        relative path, kind, owner, note, absolute path and — for a UTF-8 text file
        of at most 16 KB — the file content in a fenced block whose language tag is
        the file extension; a larger or binary file must show the path and
        "(read this file)" instead of content. Verify check_project reports a
        declared artifact that matches no file as an error whose message names the
        path, while a missing inline reference remains a warning. Verify
        command_validation substitutes `{intent_dir}` in command and expect_output.
